WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.642
Oh, hello. Welcome to our home. I’m Jo March and I’m here to share with you a little about the story you are going to read.

2
00:00:15.643 --> 00:00:19.433
As you may know, it is entitled Little Women

3
00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:26.245
. It’s a story about my family─well, more specifically, about me and my three

4
00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:33.734
sisters: Meg, who is the oldest; Beth, who is a couple of years younger than me; and the baby of the family,

5
00:00:33.735 --> 00:00:42.309
Amy. Our story is based on the true-life story of the author, Louisa May Alcott, who also had three

6
00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:47.813
sisters. Louisa May Alcott was born on November 29,

7
00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:52.702
1832. Like me, she was the second daughter in a family of four

8
00:00:52.703 --> 00:00:57.105
girls. Louisa grew up in Concord, Massachusetts,

9
00:00:57.106 --> 00:01:00.775
USA. From a young age, Louisa loved to

10
00:01:00.776 --> 00:01:05.045
write. She wrote poetry and even several thrillers, believe it or

11
00:01:05.046 --> 00:01:12.553
not. She was also an avid reader, fueling her imagination with works from Shakespeare to Charlotte

12
00:01:12.554 --> 00:01:18.774
Bronte. As you read Little Women , you may see a strong resemblance between my character

13
00:01:18.775 --> 00:01:24.393
and Louisa. In fact, according to Louisa, she did indeed base my character

14
00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:32.704
on herself, while her real sisters─Anna, Lizzie, and May─are depicted by Meg, Beth, and Amy

15
00:01:32.705 --> 00:01:36.122
respectively. Little Women was published in

16
00:01:36.123 --> 00:01:39.663
1868. The story is set during the American Civil

17
00:01:39.664 --> 00:01:44.403
War. Father is away at war, not as a soldier, but as a

18
00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:52.536
chaplain. He is a very thoughtful, kind man, who instills in us, his daughters, a strong sense of morals and family

19
00:01:52.537 --> 00:02:00.289
values. At one time Father used to be very rich but now, after the war, our family is struggling

20
00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:04.084
financially. Mother is the most loving, caring person in the

21
00:02:04.085 --> 00:02:10.341
world. She is not perfect, but she makes every effort to help us girls learn life’s important

22
00:02:10.342 --> 00:02:15.422
lessons, as well as treasure the moments we share together as a

23
00:02:15.423 --> 00:02:24.150
family. My sister Meg is a lovely person who has a strong sense of responsibility and looks after her younger

24
00:02:24.151 --> 00:02:28.767
sisters. Meg does have her faults, though, and one of them is

25
00:02:28.768 --> 00:02:34.362
vanity. She longs to have fashionable, pretty things, as most girls

26
00:02:34.363 --> 00:02:40.117
do. But what can one do if family finances don’t permit such

27
00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:46.772
treats? Next comes me. As I mentioned, the author Louisa and I share many

28
00:02:46.773 --> 00:02:50.387
traits. I am also a writer and I love to

29
00:02:50.388 --> 00:02:58.591
read. I’m not pretty like Meg or gentle like Beth, but I have a very strong personality, as my family will tell

30
00:02:58.592 --> 00:03:04.228
you. My biggest weak point is my short temper and I often lose control of

31
00:03:04.229 --> 00:03:08.997
it. It gets me into many arguments and sometimes causes

32
00:03:08.998 --> 00:03:12.262
mishaps. But I’m loyal and true to my family and

33
00:03:12.263 --> 00:03:18.699
friends. I will do anything for them. I’m a bit of a tomboy, which means I act like a

34
00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.830
boy. In fact, I’ll admit I sometimes wish I were a

35
00:03:22.831 --> 00:03:27.614
boy. This kind of thinking also gets me into

36
00:03:27.615 --> 00:03:36.640
trouble. Beth is my darling little sister. I have a soft spot for her as she is the most gentle and shy creature you will ever come

37
00:03:36.641 --> 00:03:43.343
across. Like Mother, Beth is very caring and she holds nothing back when it comes to helping others.

38
00:03:43.344 --> 00:03:52.490
Beth never complains or upsets people and she would rather do something herself than be a bother to others. She loves music.

39
00:03:52.491 --> 00:03:57.159
Her voice is as angelic as her personality.

40
00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:01.274
Finally, there’s Amy, the youngest of our clan.

41
00:04:01.275 --> 00:04:05.898
I suppose Amy and I are the pair of sisters who argue the most.

42
00:04:05.899 --> 00:04:10.070
Just between you and me, she irritates me so.

43
00:04:10.071 --> 00:04:14.416
However, I admit Amy does have her good traits.

44
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:19.273
One of them is her beauty. She is like a porcelain doll.

45
00:04:19.274 --> 00:04:23.295
When she smiles at you, you forget all your troubles.

46
00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:26.554
She is also a very talented artist.

47
00:04:26.555 --> 00:04:31.294
I wouldn’t be surprised if she became a famous painter one day.

48
00:04:31.295 --> 00:04:34.803
One of Amy’s weaknesses is her selfishness.

49
00:04:34.804 --> 00:04:38.751
She’s the youngest so I can understand this somewhat.

50
00:04:38.752 --> 00:04:46.263
But this characteristic gets her into several scrapes, which Amy thankfully learns from.

51
00:04:46.264 --> 00:04:51.895
So now you know a little about my family and something about Louisa May Alcott.

52
00:04:51.896 --> 00:04:56.974
As I mentioned before, our family lived during the American Civil War.

53
00:04:56.975 --> 00:05:01.584
Life at that time was quite different from what it is like for you today.

54
00:05:01.585 --> 00:05:05.032
For example, look at my clothes.

55
00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:14.077
Not only did we have to wear these long dresses, but when a woman went out, she was expected to wear gloves and carry a parasol.

56
00:05:14.078 --> 00:05:20.045
Given that I’m a tomboy, can you imagine how difficult it was for me to wear such things?

57
00:05:20.046 --> 00:05:25.869
My sisters had to remind me every time I wasn’t dressed in a "ladylike" way.

58
00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:31.482
At this time, women were expected to behave in a certain manner as well.

59
00:05:31.483 --> 00:05:37.307
For most women, their purpose in life consisted of finding a marriage mate and having children.

60
00:05:37.308 --> 00:05:42.292
I resisted such notions and got myself into a lot of trouble for it.

61
00:05:42.293 --> 00:05:48.529
But I, like Louisa, am a firm believer that women should have their independence.

62
00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:52.841
Another thing you might find unusual is our way of life.

63
00:05:52.842 --> 00:05:56.738
It was common in our time to have servants and housekeepers.

64
00:05:56.739 --> 00:06:01.661
My family, as well as Louisa Alcott, hated the idea of slavery.

65
00:06:01.662 --> 00:06:05.303
We would never regard our beloved Hannah as a slave.

66
00:06:05.304 --> 00:06:10.992
She is trusted and loved and is a great help to our family.

67
00:06:10.993 --> 00:06:16.618
Something else you may find peculiar is how the young men and women interact.

68
00:06:16.619 --> 00:06:20.798
In my day, society was much more conservative.

69
00:06:20.799 --> 00:06:27.260
It was not considered proper for young people to date or go out unless they intended to marry.

70
00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:36.489
It’s true that many married at a young age, but we had strict rules that allowed or did not allow certain behaviors.

71
00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:40.723
Time is constantly changing and that can’t be helped.

72
00:06:40.724 --> 00:06:44.979
Fashions, manners, customs, and traditions change, too.

73
00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:54.850
Some things, however, are timeless: learning how to grow up, learning how to deal with family issues, learning to love and respect others,

74
00:06:54.851 --> 00:07:00.882
and of course─most important of all─learning who you are.

75
00:07:00.883 --> 00:07:05.103
Little Women is a story about just those things.

76
00:07:05.104 --> 00:07:08.390
Even though it was written more than a hundred years ago,

77
00:07:08.401 --> 00:07:18.758
I hope that you will find lessons you can learn from and apply in your life today.

